    "body": "### 💡 Amaliyotdagi holat\nJava Spring Boot backend ilovasi Oracle PL/SQL dagi saqlangan protseduradan (Stored Procedure) mijozning barcha tranzaksiyalari ro'yxatini olishi kerak. Dasturchi protsedura yozdi, lekin 100 000 ta qatorni Java'ga qaytarayotganda butun serverda:\n`ORA-01000: maximum open cursors exceeded`\nxatosi chiqib, barcha ulanishlar yiqila boshladi! Kursor o'zi nima va nega u Java bilan ishlaganda to'lib ketadi?\n\n---\n\n### 1. Muammo nima? (Kursor va Private SQL Area Xotirasi)\nKursor — bu Oracle xotirasida (PGA) bajarilayotgan SQL so'rovi va uning natijalari saqlanadigan **ko'rsatkich (Pointer / Work Area)** dir.\n* **Implicit Cursor:** Har qanday oddiy `SELECT INTO`, `INSERT`, `UPDATE` paytida Oracle o'zi avtomatik ochib yopadigan kursor (`SQL%FOUND`, `SQL%ROWCOUNT`).\n* **Explicit Cursor:** Dasturchi `CURSOR c IS ... OPEN ... FETCH ... CLOSE` deb qo'lda boshqaradigan kursor.\n* **SYS_REFCURSOR (Cursor Variable):** PL/SQL ichida ochilib, natijasi Java backend'ga (yoki boshqa dasturga) ko'rsatkich sifatida uzatiladigan dinamik kursor.\n\nAgar Java backend kursor orqali ma'lumotni o'qib bo'lgach, `ResultSet` ni yopmasa (`rs.close()`), Oracle sessiyasida kursor ochiq qoladi (**Cursor Leak**). Natijada `OPEN_CURSORS` limiti (odatda 300-1000) to'lib, `ORA-01000` falokati yuz beradi.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Dasturchi uchun mental model\nOddiy massiv qaytarish — bu restoranda buyurtma qilingan 100 ta taomni bir vaqtning o'zida bitta katta stolga olib kelib tiqib qo'yishga o'xshaydi (xotira to'lib ketadi).\n**SYS_REFCURSOR** esa — bu sizga taomlar turgan oshxona eshigining kalitini (pointer) berishdir. Java backend kerak bo'lganicha taomni bittadan oladi va xohlagan paytida to'xtatadi.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Xotirada va JDBC darajasida nima sodir bo'ladi?\n```\n[ SYS_REFCURSOR va Java JDBC Bog'lanishi ]\n\nOracle DB (PL/SQL):\nOPEN p_out_cursor FOR SELECT * FROM transactions WHERE client_id = 101;\n  │\n  ▼ (Pointer uzatiladi, ma'lumotlar to'liq xotiraga yuklanmaydi!)\nJava Spring Boot (JDBC):\nCallableStatement cs = conn.prepareCall(\"{call pkg_reports.get_tx(?, ?)}\");\ncs.registerOutParameter(2, OracleTypes.CURSOR);\ncs.execute();\nResultSet rs = (ResultSet) cs.getObject(2);\nwhile (rs.next()) { ... } // Oqim tarzida (streaming) o'qiladi!\nrs.close(); // SHART! Aks holda ORA-01000 chiqadi!\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Amaliy kod va tahlili\n\nPL/SQL da `SYS_REFCURSOR` yaratish:\n```sql\nCREATE OR REPLACE PROCEDURE get_client_transactions(\n    p_client_id  IN NUMBER,\n    p_result_cur OUT SYS_REFCURSOR -- Java ga uzatiluvchi kursor o'zgaruvchisi\n) AS\nBEGIN\n    OPEN p_result_cur FOR\n        SELECT id, amount, trans_date, status\n        FROM transactions\n        WHERE client_id = p_client_id\n        ORDER BY trans_date DESC;\n    -- DIQQAT: PL/SQL da kursorni CLOSE qilmang! Uni Java yopishi shart!\nEND get_client_transactions;\n/\n```\n\nJava Spring Boot da xavfsiz qabul qilish (Try-with-resources):\n```java\n@Repository\npublic class TransactionDao {\n    @Autowired\n    private DataSource dataSource;\n\n    public List<TxDto> getTransactions(Long clientId) throws SQLException {\n        List<TxDto> list = new ArrayList<>();\n        String sql = \"{call get_client_transactions(?, ?)}\";\n\n        try (Connection conn = dataSource.getConnection();\n             CallableStatement cs = conn.prepareCall(sql)) {\n            \n            cs.setLong(1, clientId);\n            cs.registerOutParameter(2, java.sql.Types.REF_CURSOR);\n            cs.execute();\n\n            // Try-with-resources avtomatik rs.close() qiladi va Cursor Leak oldini oladi!\n            try (ResultSet rs = (ResultSet) cs.getObject(2)) {\n                while (rs.next()) {\n                    list.add(new TxDto(rs.getLong(\"id\"), rs.getBigDecimal(\"amount\")));\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        return list;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 💥 Real Production Avariyasi (Cursor Leak va ORA-01000)\nBankda monitoring tizimi har 5 soniyada bazadan hisobot olar edi. Dasturchi `ResultSet` ni `try-finally` ichida yopishni unutgan.\n* Har 5 soniyada 1 tadan kursor ochiq qolib ketdi. 1 soatda 720 ta kursor yig'ildi.\n* Natijada `ORA-01000: maximum open cursors exceeded` xatosi bilan nafaqat monitoring, balki butun bankning asosiy tranzaksiyalari to'xtab qoldi!\n* **Tekshirish:** DBA sessiyadagi ochiq kursorlarni quyidagi so'rov bilan ko'radi:\n  `SELECT * FROM v$open_cursor WHERE user_name = 'BANK_USER';`\n\n---\n\n### 🎯 Intervyuerning Tuzoqli Savoli (Trick Question)\n* **Savol:** \"PL/SQL protsedurasida ochilgan SYS_REFCURSOR'ni PL/SQL ichida CLOSE qilish kerakmi?\"\n* **Junior javobi:** \"Ha, kursor ochildimi, albatta CLOSE qilinishi shart.\"\n* **Senior javobi:** \"Yo'q! Agar siz uni PL/SQL ichida `CLOSE` qilib qo'ysangiz, Java backend'ga bo'sh va yopiq ko'rsatkich yetib boradi va Java `java.sql.SQLException: Cursor is closed` xatosini oladi. `SYS_REFCURSOR` mijozga (Java/C#) xom ashyo oqimini uzatish uchun mo'ljallangan va uni yopish mas'uliyati chaqiruvchi dastur zimmasidadir.\"\n\n---\n\n### 🗣️ Suhbatda Qanday Aytish Kerak (Speaking Template)\n> \"SYS_REFCURSOR — bu Oracle va tashqi backend (Java/Spring) o'rtasida katta hajmdagi ma'lumotlarni xotiraga to'liq yuklamasdan, oqimli (streaming) tarzda uzatishning eng samarali mexanizmidir. Bunda PL/SQL faqat pointer ochadi, uni yopish esa Java'da try-with-resources orqali ResultSet ustida bajarilishi shart. Aks holda ORA-01000 Maximum Open Cursors xatosi yuzaga keladi.\"\n\n---\n\n### 🔬 Under the Hood (Chuqur tahlil)\nOddiy explicit cursor kompilyatsiya paytida qat'iy bog'lanadi (Strongly Typed). `SYS_REFCURSOR` esa zaif bog'langan (Weakly Typed) bo'lib, ish vaqtida (runtime) istalgan SQL so'rovi bilan bog'lanishi mumkin. Uning deskriptori PGA xotirasida juda kam resurs talab qiladi va mijoz faqat talab qilingan paketlarni (fetch size bo'yicha) tarmoq orqali tortib oladi.",
